Below is a **step‑by‑step playbook** you can follow to build a modern, production‑ready frontend for an e‑commerce site.  
I’ll cover the whole stack – from design to deployment – and give you concrete code snippets, folder layouts, and tooling recommendations.  
Feel free to skip sections that already exist in your project or adapt the stack to your team’s preferences.

---

## 1. Define the Scope & Architecture

| Item | Why it matters | Typical choice |
|------|----------------|----------------|
| **Target devices** | Mobile‑first, tablet, desktop | Responsive CSS (Flexbox/Grid) |
| **SEO & SSR** | Product pages need indexable content | Next.js (React) or Nuxt.js (Vue) |
| **State management** | Cart, user session, product filters | Redux Toolkit / Zustand / React‑Query |
| **API layer** | Backend or headless CMS | REST (Axios) or GraphQL (Apollo) |
| **Payment** | Checkout flow | Stripe Elements, PayPal SDK |
| **Auth** | User login / registration | Auth0, Firebase Auth, Supabase |
| **Testing** | Unit + E2E | Jest + React Testing Library, Cypress |
| **CI/CD** | Automated deploys | GitHub Actions + Vercel / Netlify |
| **Performance** | Fast first paint | Code‑splitting, lazy‑load images, CDN |
| **Accessibility** | WCAG compliance | aXe, Lighthouse audits |

> **Tip:** Start with a **minimum viable product (MVP)** – a handful of pages (Home, Product List, Product Detail, Cart, Checkout) – then iterate.

---

## 2. Design & Prototyping

1. **Wireframe** – Sketch low‑fidelity screens in Figma or Sketch.  
2. **Design System** – Create reusable components (buttons, cards, modals).  
3. **Style Guide** – Define colors, typography, spacing, and component states.  
4. **Export assets** – SVG icons, product thumbnails, hero images.

> **Tooling:**  
> • **Figma** (free tier) – collaborative design.  
> • **Storybook** – document components in isolation.  
> • **Tailwind CSS** – utility‑first styling that speeds up prototyping.

---

## 3. Project Setup

### 3.1. Choose a Framework

| Framework | Strengths | Example Boilerplate |
|-----------|-----------|---------------------|
| **Next.js** (React) | SSR, ISR, file‑based routing, API routes | `npx create-next-app@latest ecommerce-frontend` |
| **Nuxt.js** (Vue) | SSR, Vuex, composables | `npx nuxi init ecommerce-frontend` |
| **SvelteKit** | Tiny bundle, reactive stores | `npm init svelte@next ecommerce-frontend` |

> **Recommendation:** Next.js if you’re comfortable with React; Nuxt if you prefer Vue; SvelteKit for the smallest bundle.

### 3.2. Add TypeScript

```bash
# Next.js
npx create-next-app@latest ecommerce-frontend --typescript
```

### 3.3. Install Core Dependencies

```bash
cd ecommerce-frontend
npm install axios react-query @tanstack/react-query
npm install tailwindcss postcss autoprefixer
npx tailwindcss init -p
```

> **Optional:**  
> • `@heroicons/react` for icons  
> • `react-hook-form` for form handling  
> • `zod` for schema validation

### 3.4. Folder Structure

```
/src
  /components   # UI primitives (Button, Card, Modal)
  /pages        # Next.js pages (index.tsx, product/[slug].tsx, cart.tsx)
  /hooks        # Custom hooks (useCart, useAuth)
  /lib          # API clients, utilities
  /styles       # Tailwind config, global.css
  /assets       # Images, icons
  /context      # React Contexts (AuthContext, CartContext)
  /tests        # Jest + React Testing Library
```

---

## 4. Core Features Implementation

### 4.1. Routing & Navigation

```tsx
// src/pages/_app.tsx
import '../styles/globals.css';
import type { AppProps } from 'next/app';
import { QueryClient, QueryClientProvider } from '@tanstack/react-query';
import { CartProvider } from '@/context/CartContext';

const queryClient = new QueryClient();

export default function MyApp({ Component, pageProps }: AppProps) {
  return (
    <QueryClientProvider client={queryClient}>
      <CartProvider>
        <Component {...pageProps} />
      </CartProvider>
    </QueryClientProvider>
  );
}
```

### 4.2. API Client

```ts
// src/lib/api.ts
import axios from 'axios';

const api = axios.create({
  baseURL: process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL,
  headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },
});

export const fetchProducts = async () => {
  const { data } = await api.get('/products');
  return data;
};

export const fetchProductBySlug = async (slug: string) => {
  const { data } = await api.get(`/products/${slug}`);
  return data;
};
```

### 4.3. Product List Page

```tsx
// src/pages/index.tsx
import { useQuery } from '@tanstack/react-query';
import { fetchProducts } from '@/lib/api';
import ProductCard from '@/components/ProductCard';

export default function Home() {
  const { data, isLoading, error } = useQuery(['products'], fetchProducts);

  if (isLoading) return <p>Loading…</p>;
  if (error) return <p>Something went wrong.</p>;

  return (
    <div className="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-4 gap-6 p-4">
      {data.map((product: any) => (
        <ProductCard key={product.id} product={product} />
      ))}
    </div>
  );
}
```

### 4.4. Product Detail Page

```tsx
// src/pages/product/[slug].tsx
import { useRouter } from 'next/router';
import { useQuery } from '@tanstack/react-query';
import { fetchProductBySlug } from '@/lib/api';
import { useCart } from '@/hooks/useCart';

export default function ProductDetail() {
  const router = useRouter();
  const { slug } = router.query;
  const { data, isLoading, error } = useQuery(
    ['product', slug],
    () => fetchProductBySlug(slug as string),
    { enabled: !!slug }
  );
  const { addToCart } = useCart();

  if (isLoading) return <p>Loading…</p>;
  if (error) return <p>Product not found.</p>;

  return (
    <div className="flex flex-col md:flex-row gap-8 p-4">
      <img src={data.imageUrl} alt={data.title} className="w-full md:w-1/2 object-cover" />
      <div className="md:w-1/2">
        <h1 className="text-3xl font-bold">{data.title}</h1>
        <p className="mt-4 text-xl text-green-600">${data.price}</p>
        <p className="mt-6">{data.description}</p>
        <button
          onClick={() => addToCart(data)}
          className="mt-8 bg-blue-600 text-white px-6 py-3 rounded hover:bg-blue-700"
        >
          Add to Cart
        </button>
      </div>
    </div>
  );
}
```

### 4.5. Cart Context & Hook

```tsx
// src/context/CartContext.tsx
import { createContext, useContext, useReducer } from 'react';

type CartItem = { id: string; quantity: number; price: number };
type State = { items: CartItem[] };
type Action =
  | { type: 'ADD'; item: CartItem }
  | { type: 'REMOVE'; id: string }
  | { type: 'CLEAR' };

const reducer = (state: State, action: Action): State => {
  switch (action.type) {
    case 'ADD':
      const existing = state.items.find(i => i.id === action.item.id);
      if (existing) {
        return {
          items: state.items.map(i =>
            i.id === action.item.id ? { ...i, quantity: i.quantity + action.item.quantity } : i
          ),
        };
      }
      return { items: [...state.items, action.item] };
    case 'REMOVE':
      return { items: state.items.filter(i => i.id !== action.id) };
    case 'CLEAR':
      return { items: [] };
    default:
      return state;
  }
};

const CartContext = createContext<{
  state: State;
  dispatch: React.Dispatch<Action>;
}>({ state: { items: [] }, dispatch: () => null });

export const CartProvider = ({ children }: { children: React.ReactNode }) => {
  const [state, dispatch] = useReducer(reducer, { items: [] });
  return <CartContext.Provider value={{ state, dispatch }}>{children}</CartContext.Provider>;
};

export const useCart = () => {
  const { state, dispatch } = useContext(CartContext);
  const addToCart = (item: CartItem) => dispatch({ type: 'ADD', item });
  const removeFromCart = (id: string) => dispatch({ type: 'REMOVE', id });
  const clearCart = () => dispatch({ type: 'CLEAR' });
  return { ...state, addToCart, removeFromCart, clearCart };
};
```

### 4.6. Checkout Flow

1. **Cart Summary** – Show items, subtotal, shipping estimate.  
2. **Billing & Shipping Form** – Use `react-hook-form` + `zod`.  
3. **Payment** – Embed Stripe Elements or PayPal Buttons.  
4. **Order Confirmation** – Render a success page and send a webhook to your backend.

```tsx
// src/pages/checkout.tsx
import { useCart } from '@/hooks/useCart';
import { useForm } from 'react-hook-form';
import { z } from 'zod';
import { zodResolver } from '@hookform/resolvers/zod';
import { loadStripe } from '@stripe/stripe-js';
import { Elements, CardElement, useStripe, useElements } from '@stripe/react-stripe-js';

const stripePromise = loadStripe(process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_STRIPE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY!);

const schema = z.object({
  name: z.string().min(1),
  email: z.string().email(),
  address: z.string().min(1),
});

export default function Checkout() {
  const { items, clearCart } = useCart();
  const { register, handleSubmit, formState: { errors } } = useForm({
    resolver: zodResolver(schema),
  });

  const onSubmit = async (data: any) => {
